{
	title: 'Prompt-file change notices, scoped to the project',
	spec: 'When a file the system prompt reads changes, the user sees a notice popup (the qm stack), never a scrollback line, so scrollback does not fill with them. SYSTEM.md and the files it includes (they bust the prompt cache the same way) go to every client watching a tab. An AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md change goes only to clients whose shown tab it applies to: the file sits in a directory from that tab cwd up to its Git root (systemPrompt.candidates), so a project AGENTS.md shows only in tabs inside that project. The notice names the file, says changed, created or deleted, and gives its path; one notice per path replaces the previous, so repeated saves show once. Opening a tab or starting the host announces nothing: a file is compared only with what the host saw before. The host checks these files about once a second while clients watch tabs (src/host/prompt-files.ts), and only the host does. Test: a change reaches the tabs it applies to and no others; SYSTEM.md reaches all.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Polls (readFileSync per pass) instead of fs.watch: the watched set follows which tab each client shows and its cwd, and editors save by rename; comparing contents also ignores touches. Uses the update kind (neutral colour) with what = changed/created/deleted and key prompt-file:<path>; session is the receiving client's shown tab, so a web tap stays put. Not recorded in notice history: entries need a session and these are not about one. Files SYSTEM.md includes are not watched.",
		'Watched set per shown tab = systemPrompt.inspect sources (SYSTEM.md, its includes, present AGENTS.md) plus every AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md candidate, so creation is seen too; a missing optional @? include is not. Every detection and delivery goes to diag.log as "prompt files: ...". An edit made before the host starts is its baseline and is never announced: the first report of "nothing happens" was a SYSTEM.md saved before the restart that loaded this code.',
		'Latency: a terminal without focus is not "visible", so prompt-file notices waited for focus. host.ts records `shown` (the tab a client shows, focused or not) and prompt-files routes by it; fs.watch on the watched files\' directories (renames by editors included) triggers a check within 30 ms, the 1 s poll remains for tab and cwd changes.'
	],
	needs: ['qm', '29']
}
